 the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}=-2\\cdot (-1)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "898de07e-22f0-5b81-a6cd-37d35343a1b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155542} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac8670e-07ad-5f8d-ac5e-7bfe6a35b537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155543} {:answer/id #uuid "c143d4fe-69e7-5420-9ea9-3d38db56c785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155544} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1a88aa-b632-5b2b-8f59-780e088a5400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155545} 